 "notes": "Joy-Con 2 (L/R) of Nintendo Switch 2 over USB. The HID report descriptor is the real device's 100 bytes, byte for byte, from switch2_controller_research (descriptors.md, Joy-Con 2 (L)); the right half differs only in Report ID (8 instead of 7). Two input reports are built from the 24-byte state block. 0x05, the common report, carries the counter, the buttons at data[6]/data[7], both 12-bit packed sticks at data[11:14]/data[14:17] and the Motion Data block at data[0x2B:] — the offsets SDL's switch2 driver reads (SDL_hidapi_switch2.c HandleMiniControllerStateL and the sensor block of HandleSwitchProState). 0x07/0x08, the structured report, carries the buttons at data[3:5] in the real device's Button Format order and the stick at data[6:9], so the plain HID path (browser Gamepad API, DirectInput, Windows GameInput) can parse the Button usages the descriptor declares. No vendor interface and no command protocol: the device streams reports from the first frame."
